  "system": {
    "category": "path",
    "identifier": "soul-smith",
    "source": "Bad Eden (2024 rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>\"Give me time, a fire, and something to hit — and then we'll see.\"</em></p>\n<p>The Soul-Smith runs a forge that does not much care whether you call it a person or a furnace; it answers to heat and intention either way. Mechanically you ride <strong>Burn</strong> — a 0→8 heat track that climbs when you or a nearby ally takes a hit (the forge stokes itself on other people's bad days) and banks <strong>Surge</strong> right alongside it. You spend that Surge on four forge-works, and the hotter you run, the harder they land — right up until the furnace bites back.</p>\n<h3>The Four Works (spent via Surge)</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Forge-Weld.</strong> Lay hands on the breakage and repair an ally — 1d8 + tier integrity. <em>Stoked</em> (Burn 2–3) ×1.5; <em>Overheated</em> (Burn 4+) ×2, and Overheated also costs you 1d6 Stress, because an open forge has opinions about being grabbed.</li>\n  <li><strong>Atonement Crucible.</strong> Cleanse a condition off an ally (two while Stoked or hotter) and temper the wound into armor — they gain DR equal to your tier. The bad thing that happened to them is now load-bearing.</li>\n  <li><strong>Furnace of Renewal.</strong> Light the aura: allies within 6 squares heal (Burn-scaled) and share your poison/qliphothic resistance for three rounds. Stand near the fire. It is rude not to.</li>\n  <li><strong>Relic of Rebirth.</strong> Forge a ward on an ally — the next hit that would drop them is held at 1. While Overheated, instead reforge a fallen ally back to half integrity (once per fight). The forge does not accept \"dead\" as a final answer. It considers it a draft.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Vent</strong> to cool Burn. Out of combat, <strong>Forge Works</strong> still does the slow miracles — repairing hexes, purifying corrupted Sparks, restoring ruined regions. Those take time, the way good welds do.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
